1
00:00:00,306 --> 00:00:03,346
Okay, it's lame when I say it,
it's ridiculous when you pile on.

2
00:00:03,518 --> 00:00:05,598
(Leonard:)Okay. Sorry.

3
00:00:05,770 --> 00:00:08,310
(Penny:)What did she say
when you told her we were going out?

4
00:00:08,481 --> 00:00:09,811
LEONARD:
Um....

5
00:00:10,358 --> 00:00:12,648
(Penny:)You didn't tell her we were going out,
did you?

6
00:00:12,819 --> 00:00:14,319
LEONARD:
Um....

7
00:00:14,487 --> 00:00:17,367
(Penny:)-Why not?
-Um....

8
00:00:17,532 --> 00:00:19,362
(Sheldon:)Leonard,
I'm no expert on meditation...

9
00:00:19,534 --> 00:00:23,124
(Sheldon:)...but if you're trying to calm yourself
down, I believe the word is "om."

10
00:00:26,708 --> 00:00:29,668
(Beverley:)It was so nice of you
to come to the airport to pick me up.

11
00:00:29,836 --> 00:00:31,296
(Sheldon:)No trouble at all.

12
00:00:31,462 --> 00:00:33,882
(Leonard:)I drove, Mother.

13
00:00:34,882 --> 00:00:36,512
(Leonard:)I'm driving now.

14
00:00:36,676 --> 00:00:38,006
(Beverley:)Yes, dear. Mommy's proud.

15
00:00:39,554 --> 00:00:43,724
(Beverley:)Thank you for your notes on my paper
disproving quantum-brain-dynamic theory.

16
00:00:43,933 --> 00:00:44,973
(Sheldon:)My pleasure.

17
00:00:45,143 --> 00:00:48,233
You know, for a non-physicist,
you have a remarkable grasp...

18
00:00:48,438 --> 00:00:51,318
(Sheldon:)...of how electric dipoles
in the brain's water molecules...

19
00:00:51,482 --> 00:00:53,652
(Sheldon:)...could not possibly form
a Bose condensate.

20
00:00:54,068 --> 00:00:58,068
(Leonard:)Wait, wait, wait. When did you
send my mom notes on a paper?

21
00:00:58,239 --> 00:01:03,019
(Sheldon:)August 16th.
Right after her carpal-tunnel surgery.

